@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "DevOps Lifecycle";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Understanding the DevOps lifecycle helps organizations streamline software development, deployment, and monitoring processes.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- DevOps Lifecycle Overview -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-primary">Stages of DevOps Lifecycle</h2>
        <p>
            The DevOps lifecycle consists of various stages, each playing a critical role in ensuring continuous software delivery and operational excellence. These stages are interdependent and follow an iterative process.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>1. Plan:</strong> Teams define project goals, requirements, and roadmaps using Agile methodologies and collaboration tools like Jira and Trello.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>2. Develop:</strong> Developers write code using version control systems (Git, GitHub, GitLab) and follow best coding practices.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>3. Build:</strong> The code is compiled, tested, and packaged using CI/CD tools like Jenkins, GitHub Actions, and Travis CI.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>4. Test:</strong> Automated testing (unit, integration, performance) is performed using frameworks like Selenium, JUnit, and Jest.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>5. Release:</strong> The final product is prepared for deployment, ensuring smooth and error-free rollouts with feature toggles and blue-green deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>6. Deploy:</strong> The software is deployed into production using tools like Kubernetes, Docker, and Terraform.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>7. Operate:</strong> Continuous monitoring and maintenance are performed using observability tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK Stack.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>8. Monitor:</strong> Real-time logging and analytics help detect anomalies, security vulnerabilities, and performance issues.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/devops-lifecycle.png" alt="DevOps Lifecycle" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>The DevOps lifecycle ensures seamless and efficient software development and deployment.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Benefits of DevOps Lifecycle -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-success">Why Follow the DevOps Lifecycle?</h2>
        <p>
            Implementing the DevOps lifecycle improves efficiency, reduces deployment risks, and enhances collaboration between teams.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Continuous Improvement:</strong> Iterative feedback loops ensure constant enhancements and bug fixes.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Faster Time-to-Market:</strong> Automating workflows reduces release cycles and accelerates software delivery.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enhanced Security:</strong> DevSecOps integrates security best practices early in the development cycle.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Reliability & Scalability:</strong> Cloud-native deployments ensure high availability and fault tolerance.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            The DevOps lifecycle bridges the gap between development and operations, enabling faster innovation, better quality software, and seamless deployments. Organizations that adopt DevOps methodologies experience increased productivity and improved customer satisfaction.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/devops-continuous.png" alt="DevOps Continuous Lifecycle" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>DevOps is a continuous and evolving process, driving efficiency in IT operations.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
